 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Rational Tate module of a divisible abelian group",
 "statement": "Let $M$ be an abelian group, let $\\ell$ be a prime, and let $r$ be a natural number. If multiplication by $\\ell$ is surjective on $M$ and $\\operatorname{Nat.card}(M[\\ell])=\\ell^r$, then the rational Tate module $V_\\ell M$ of [def-tate-module-abelian-group] is nonempty-linearly-equivalent over $\\mathbb Q_\\ell$ to $(\\mathbb Q_\\ell)^r$.",
 "source": {
